# Rank 1294 / CVE-2024-23649: Lemmy's private-message report endpoint
# (`create_pm_report` in crates/api/src/private_message_report/create.rs)
# read the target private message by the caller-supplied
# `private_message_id` and immediately built a `PrivateMessageReportForm`
# from it, with no check that the requesting user is the message's
# recipient. Any authenticated user could therefore file a report against
# a private message addressed to someone else -- including the sender's
# own outgoing message -- disclosing its content to admins via
# `PrivateMessageReportView` and the report-email path (CWE-862).
#
# Fix commit bc32b408b523b9b64aa57b8e47748f96cce0dae5 ("Fixing private
# message reports.", #4279) adds, right after the `PrivateMessage::read`
# lookup and before the report form is built: `if person_id !=
# private_message.recipient_id { Err(LemmyErrorType::CouldntCreateReport)? }`.
# The rest of the diff (api_tests/src/private_message.spec.ts,
# api_tests/src/shared.ts) is TypeScript integration-test scaffolding for
# the new check, not part of the vulnerable or fixed code itself -- despite
# the pool row's "typescript" language, the actual fix lives entirely in
# Rust; the row names rust.
#
# ATTENTION, vocabulary gap. `vyql explain` on a verbatim repro of
# `create_pm_report` reports no findings on either revision; `vyql match`
# labels only the three `data.*` field reads as code.Param/code.ExternalEntryInput
# (library.param-source) and nothing else -- `PrivateMessage::read` and
# `PrivateMessageReport::report` are not bound as anything, so no rule can
# see this function at all. A bounded scan of the real repository (--cache
# off --max-ram 5GB) reports 44 findings, none in private_message_report/
# or naming private_message anywhere.
#
# code.IdorPolicyReview ("review object lookup or delete criteria for a
# current-principal ownership constraint") is the nearest concept by theme
# -- this is exactly an object lookup (`PrivateMessage::read`) whose result
# feeds a mutating action with no current-principal ownership check -- but
# it has no Rust binding today, only PHP and JavaScript ones, and every
# existing binding for it (see rank1146's ledger note for the same gap in
# Java) is a hardcoded per-CVE structural match in that language's
# treesitter frontend (`phpReview`/JS `callPath`+`identifier` literals)
# rather than a general Rust pattern computed from the AST. Adding
# a Rust one would mean writing a new `rust_review` fact in
# internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/rust.go recognizing "a `Type::read`
# call followed by a mutating call built from its result, with no
# comparison between one of the read struct's fields and the current
# principal in between" -- a new classification, not a correction to an
# existing switch case, and exactly the kind of design call rank1146 also
# declined to make inside this loop. No definition change attempted.
#
# Rechecked on the current knowledge base; the miss holds, and the blocker
# decomposes into one fact that has since changed and two that have not.
# (1) The source half of VYQL-AUTH-002 is now present: the Library/SDK
# profile's param-source labels every public-API parameter of
# `create_pm_report` as `code.ExternalEntryInput`, which refines
# `core.UserControlledData`, so the request-derived `private_message_id` is
# a live taint source on this tree. What is missing is only the sink.
# (2) The Rust `code.ObjectLookupByUserInput` set binds the generic
# by-identity spellings `find_by_id`, `get_user` and `get_account`
# (bindings/rust/mdc4f74cd.vyql), not Lemmy's own `Crud::read(pool, id)`
# accessor. Binding `callee.method == "read"` at args[1] was measured on the
# real checkout: it takes the tree from 44 findings to 140, of which 96 are
# VYQL-AUTH-002 rows landing on ~50 files (`read_community.rs` reading a
# public community by id, `post/like.rs`, `build_response.rs`, every
# `*_report/resolve.rs`) for one true positive -- and the fixed revision
# reports the identical 140 findings and 96 rows, so the binding buys no
# discrimination at all. The reachable set is the reason: exhaustive grep
# counts 237 `X::read(`/`.read(` calls in lemmy (59 of them the
# `X::read(&mut context.pool(), <arg>)` handler form, across 20 distinct
# types, most of them public objects), 572 in uv, 448 in kata-containers,
# 186 in wasmtime, 144 in grin, 127 in zeptoclaw, because `read` is also
# std's `Read::read`. Which of those types holds private content is not in
# the code.
# (3) The rule's `unless endpoint coveredBy core.OwnershipCheck` half cannot
# be satisfied by this fix under any generic binding: the Rust
# `core.OwnershipCheck` set is `check_ownership` and `require_owner` only,
# and the fix is a bare inline `if person_id != private_message.recipient_id`
# with no named API at all -- the comparison's left side comes from
# `local_user_view.person.id` and its right side from a field of the row
# just read, and neither the field name nor the guard's absence is a
# contract. Keying the neutraliser on `recipient_id` would encode the fixing
# commit's own vocabulary, and a sibling handler that delegates the same
# comparison to a helper stays invisible (the Rust delegated-check gap).
# Both revisions of the full tree still scan identically at 44 findings,
# 19 at or above high, 3 x `--cache off` runs each, with zero findings in
# crates/api/src/private_message_report/ on either side.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-vocabulary-gap, both revisions reject
# code.IdorPolicyReview (nearest review concept by theme; no Rust binding
# exists for it, and the rule that would consume a lookup sink cannot
# separate the fixed revision either).

test "rank1294: report creation trusts the caller-supplied private_message_id with no recipient check"
  lang rust
  file create.rs
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  pub async fn create_pm_report(
    data: Json<CreatePrivateMessageReport>,
    context: Data<LemmyContext>,
    local_user_view: LocalUserView,
  ) -> Result<Json<PrivateMessageReportResponse>, LemmyError> {
    let local_site = LocalSite::read(&mut context.pool()).await?;

    let reason = data.reason.trim().to_string();
    check_report_reason(&reason, &local_site)?;

    let person_id = local_user_view.person.id;
    let private_message_id = data.private_message_id;
    let private_message = PrivateMessage::read(&mut context.pool(), private_message_id).await?;

    let report_form = PrivateMessageReportForm {
      creator_id: person_id,
      private_message_id,
      original_pm_text: private_message.content,
      reason,
    };

    let report = PrivateMessageReport::report(&mut context.pool(), &report_form)
      .await
      .with_lemmy_type(LemmyErrorType::CouldntCreateReport)?;

    let private_message_report_view =
      PrivateMessageReportView::read(&mut context.pool(), report.id).await?;

    Ok(Json(PrivateMessageReportResponse {
      private_message_report_view,
    }))
  }
  ```

test "rank1294: report creation rejects a caller who is not the message's recipient"
  lang rust
  file create.rs
  reject_review code.IdorPolicyReview
  code
  ```
  pub async fn create_pm_report(
    data: Json<CreatePrivateMessageReport>,
    context: Data<LemmyContext>,
    local_user_view: LocalUserView,
  ) -> Result<Json<PrivateMessageReportResponse>, LemmyError> {
    let local_site = LocalSite::read(&mut context.pool()).await?;

    let reason = data.reason.trim().to_string();
    check_report_reason(&reason, &local_site)?;

    let person_id = local_user_view.person.id;
    let private_message_id = data.private_message_id;
    let private_message = PrivateMessage::read(&mut context.pool(), private_message_id).await?;

    if person_id != private_message.recipient_id {
      Err(LemmyErrorType::CouldntCreateReport)?
    }

    let report_form = PrivateMessageReportForm {
      creator_id: person_id,
      private_message_id,
      original_pm_text: private_message.content,
      reason,
    };

    let report = PrivateMessageReport::report(&mut context.pool(), &report_form)
      .await
      .with_lemmy_type(LemmyErrorType::CouldntCreateReport)?;

    let private_message_report_view =
      PrivateMessageReportView::read(&mut context.pool(), report.id).await?;

    Ok(Json(PrivateMessageReportResponse {
      private_message_report_view,
    }))
  }
  ```
